Access the head node by any of the following:

(1) ParallelClusterMaker access script:
    ./access_cluster.py -N {{ cluster_name }}

(2) ParallelCluster CLI:
    pcluster ssh --cluster-name {{ cluster_name }} -i {{ ssh_keypair }}

(3) ssh with the cluster's private key:
    ssh -i {{ ssh_keypair }} {{ ec2_user }}@{{ head_node_public_ip }}

Compute nodes idle for more than {{ scaledown_idletime }} minutes are
terminated automatically, so an idle cluster scales its compute fleet
to zero on its own. The head node keeps running and billing until the
cluster is destroyed.

Nothing tears this cluster down on a timer. Destroy it with:

$ ./kill_pcluster.py -N {{ cluster_name }} -O {{ cluster_owner }} -A {{ az }}

